<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v7">
<!--
    GH-5897: "Ghidra Uses pre-UAL Syntax for register-to-register movs in armv7 le"
    https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/5897

    Bytes 07 c0 a0 e1 (word 0xe1a0c007) are a register-to-register MOV
    (MOV r12,r7).  SLEIGH matched the pre-UAL ":cpy^COND Rd,rm" constructor and
    rendered the deprecated mnemonic "cpy r12,r7" instead of the modern UAL
    "mov r12,r7".  Other MOV forms in the same binary already render UAL "mov".

    Stage: S1 decode-table (SLEIGH spec-fix, no option).  The fix renames the
    register-copy ":cpy^COND Rd,rm" / ":cpy^COND lr,rm" constructor mnemonics to
    "mov" (the UAL synonym; identical p-code).  This testcase pins the FIXED
    mnemonic and forbids the deprecated "cpy" token.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x0">
07c0a0e1
</bytechunk>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>disassemble 0x0 0x4</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="GH5897 #1: reg-to-reg MOV renders UAL 'mov r12,r7'" min="1" max="1">^0x00000000: mov[ ]+r12,r7</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="GH5897 #2: deprecated pre-UAL 'cpy' mnemonic is gone" min="0" max="0">\bcpy\b</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
